WEALTH DEFINITION
According to Adam Smith,
'Economics is the science of wealth'.
But in economics, the term wealth' has a special
meaning. In Economics, wealth refers to those goods
which satisfy human wants.
Adam Smith was of the view that economics is
concerned with the problems arising from wealthgetting and wealth-using activities of people.
He was interested mainly in studying the ways by, which the wealth of all nations could be increased.
However, welfare definition was criticized as it
gave too much importance to material wealth and
ignored human welfare and moral values.
