ECONOMIC AND NON-ECONOMIC ACTIVITIES
Economic Activities
Economic activities refer to those activities, which
are undertaken to earn a living.
Economic activities are concerned with all those
activities, which are concerned with the Production,
Consumption and Distribution of goods and services,
which are not available for free. So, every economy
should undertake three main economic activities:
Consumption: Consumption is an economic activity which deals with the
use of goods and services for the satisfaction of human wants.) Eating of
bread, drinking of milk, wearing watches, listening music, etc. are
consumption activities. In consumption, we study wants, their origin, nature
and characteristics and the laws governing them.
